      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Shared docs of the TSX service classes dropped in the split** (`crates/rayx_app_nsh/src/services/mod.rs:1-4`, each `services/*/*_ts.rs:1`).\n\nExpected: t02 keeps each item's docs; the split of `ts/services.rs` keeps what its module doc said about every class it held. Observed: `git show HEAD:crates/rayx_app_nsh/src/ts/services.rs` lines 1-7 (each class carries its Rust service's name and is its own token; each `onChange` listener hears changes until its returned function is called, its reactive owner goes or the object is disposed; values cross as plain objects, the services' snapshots serialized; the services notify on the engine's thread, where TSX listeners run) appear nowhere in the tree: the new files say only \"The X service for TSX.\" (`ts/options.rs`' and `platform.rs`' module docs were carried over into `configuration/options_ts.rs`, `configuration_builder_ts.rs`, `snapshot.rs`, `sync.rs`, `reader.rs`, `registrar.rs`; this one was not).\n\nRepair: move that paragraph (with the `I18nService` link pointed at `crate::ts::I18nService`) into the module doc of `services/mod.rs`, where the shared `json()` helper the classes use now lives, or into `ts.rs`' list of the services' classes.\n\nResolved: `services/mod.rs`'s module doc now carries HEAD's paragraph (own token, `onChange` lifetime, plain objects, engine-thread notifications) with `crate::ts::I18nService`.",
      "regressionRefs": [
