      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**`NshServicesAppBuilderExt`'s documented home moved off the crate root** (`crates/rayx_app_nsh/src/lib.rs:120`, `crates/rayx_app_nsh/src/services/mod.rs:52`).\n\nExpected (LAYOUT-2, no public path change): the trait is documented where it was, `rayx_app_nsh::NshServicesAppBuilderExt` (`target/doc/rayx_app_nsh/trait.NshServicesAppBuilderExt.html`), as at HEAD, when it sat in the private `platform` module and rustdoc inlined the root re-export. Observed: d-layout puts it in `services/mod.rs`, and choice (a) made `services` a `pub mod`, so the trait gained a second public path `rayx_app_nsh::services::NshServicesAppBuilderExt` and rustdoc no longer inlines the root re-export: after `cargo doc -p rayx_app_nsh --no-deps`, `target/doc/rayx_app_nsh/trait.NshServicesAppBuilderExt.html` is gone, only `services/trait.NshServicesAppBuilderExt.html` exists, and the root lists the trait under Re-exports. Rust paths still resolve (`rayx_app_nsh::NshServicesAppBuilderExt`, the `rayx` prelude), so no code breaks. It is the only item that changed this way: every other root re-export comes from a `pub(crate)` submodule and is still inlined.\n\nRepair: put `#[doc(inline)]` on `pub use services::NshServicesAppBuilderExt;` in `lib.rs`, so the root page is generated again. The extra path `services::NshServicesAppBuilderExt` follows from d-layout's table plus choice (a) and goes away when s4 removes the trait. Note it in the commit body rather than moving the trait out of `services/mod.rs`.\n\nResolved: `#[doc(inline)]` on the root re-export (`lib.rs:120-121`); `target/doc/rayx_app_nsh/trait.NshServicesAppBuilderExt.html` is generated again.",
